From: Kettle Linux <noreply@kettlelinux>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ch13726a: wait 120 ms after sleep-out

The DDIC needs 120 ms after SLPOUT before DISPON (MIPI DCS). ROCKNIX's SM8250
copy of this driver (used by the RP5) carries the delay; the
SM8550 copy in 20-sm8550 does not.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
index ae29144..34a7cd2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@ static int ch13726a_on(struct ch13726a_panel *ctx)
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xb9, 0x00);
 	
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_exit_sleep_mode_multi(&dsi_ctx);
+	mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, 120);
 
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_on_multi(&dsi_ctx);
 
